ck_id": "est2", "hash": "5b53886125677fe01c7c131e2407fe7b", "replacement_id": "d224713e-da71-5966-81d2-910764d7cd04", "disposition": "archived_source_defect", "reason": "The source distractor J reads ∞ < x < −2; complete original choice evidence is unavailable. A separately labeled instructor practice version supplies complete choices."}], "question": {"id": "d224713e-da71-5966-81d2-910764d7cd04", "track_id": "est2", "topic": "Exponents, radicals and growth", "difficulty": "hard", "type": "mcq", "stem": "Instructor-reviewed practice. The graph shows an increasing exponential function f with f(−2) = 16. Which choice describes the complete set of real x for which f(x) > 16?", "choices": [{"key": "F", "text": "x > −2"}, {"key": "G", "text": "x > 0"}, {"key": "H", "text": "−2 < x < 2"}, {"key": "J", "text": "x < −2"}], "correct": "F", "explanation": "Because f is strictly increasing and f(−2) = 16, values to the right of x = −2 give f(x) > 16; values to the left give f(x) < 16. At x = −2 there is equality, so the endpoint is excluded. The complete solution is x > −2 (F). G and H omit valid values; J is on the wrong side. The original graph is retained. J is an instructor-authored distractor, not a claim about the unavailable original choice typography.", "assets": {"source": "Eng. Abdelrahman Ghoneem — instructor-reviewed practice", "source_code": "GH-EST2-EXP-GRAPH-20261015", "source_question_id": "GH-EST2-EXP-GRAPH-20261015", "content_origin": "instructor_adaptation", "adapted_from_question_id": "f3c606d2-2273-58b1-97db-44fd0e92b79b", "adaptation_reason": "Source markdown has an incomplete infinity-sign distractor. Complete, explicit practice choices are authored separately; the original remains archived.", "source_archive_library_id": "libfile_bf57f23ca344819199a3207a9fbcf774", "original_source_file": "moh.md", "original_source_sha256": "f99122153ba873fb3a01697b0501e31119af3babff6a9ed2bc0baf050aed1f20", "original_image_sha256": "2d963a4bae738b9c145bfaf3c45633a8acf573