on_id": "fdb00d7a-f3b3-5ee3-ad95-73d30e5a838c", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "1+2+3+4+5=15; also 5*6/2=15.", "updated_at": "2026-09-11 03:21:07.665036+00", "hash": "6082095461b29910d0c8b5a08f10301e", "status": "excluded", "note": "1+2+3+4+5=15; also 5*6/2=15.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "clean:PSD 132", "track_id": "est", "source_code": "PSD 132", "question_id": "1b9f821a-f99f-5ea7-8f1d-97f2c4ce6217", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original PDF visually checked; isolated complete question and independently verified the solution.\nWorked solution: The model is 6000(1+r)⁸=8950.95. At r=0.05, the amount is 6000·1.05⁸≈8950.95. Thus the rate is 5%.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 21:08:45.167383+00", "hash": "f7d472e90968a91595ee2a7253100045", "status": "needs_source_repair", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original PDF visually checked; isolated complete question and independently verified the solution.\nWorked solution: The model is 6000(1+r)⁸=8950.95. At r=0.05, the amount is 6000·1.05⁸≈8950.95. Thus the rate is 5%.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Original source remains archived; use the separately verified explicit-rounding practice adaptation. A ready archive label must not override live eligibility."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2dec:q37", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-DEC2020-Q37", "question_id": "8bd77556-4760-58d9-b07b-93aeba048af6", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Added the required positive-integer restriction.\nWorked solution: Since 6!=720, the fraction is 12m/720=m/60. It is an integer exactly when m is a multiple of 60. The least positive such integer is 60.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:46.271902+00", "hash": "a9803f414bfc6d6f320be061fdd0f7cd", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Added the required positive-integer restriction.\nWorked solution: Since 6!=720, the fraction is 12m/720=m/60. It is an integer exactly when m is a multiple of 60. The least positive such integer is 60.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2june:q02", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-JUN2021-Q02", "question_id": "dc963911-a748-5368-a85d-40227434e37c", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Corrected the printed −1.65 rounding to −1.66, consistently across the distractors, and stated the rounding precision.\nWorked solution: Unit length requires 1/16+(3m+4)²=1. Hence 3m+4=±√15/4 and m=(−16±√15)/12. The roots are approximately −1.010585 and −1.656082, which round to −1.01 and −1.66.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:46.271902+00", "hash": "7e0c7961a11c1ea20b0f9a1547c1a578", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Corrected the printed −1.65 rounding to −1.66, consistently across the distractors, and stated the rounding precision.\nWorked solution: Unit length requires 1/16+(3m+4)²=1. Hence 3m+4=±√15/4 and m=(−16±√15)/12. The roots are approximately −1.010585 and −1.656082, which round to −1.01 and −1.66.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2june:q15", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-JUN2021-Q15", "question_id": "0bd86cbf-8704-54be-8c51-08d98401913f", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Restored the source graph and scoped the question to the three line formulas, which uniquely identify E without assuming missing endpoint markers.\nWorked solution: The left segment has slope 1 and passes through (−3,0), giving y=x+3. The middle segment has slope 2 and y-intercept −1, giving y=2x−1. The right segment has slope −1/2 and passes through (4,0), giving y=−x/2+2. Only E has all three expressions. The source does not mark endpoint inclusion clearly, so the prompt deliberately asks about the segments away from the breakpoints.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:47.350971+00", "hash": "5dc1607633c10c7d9f54ccb84d0bec55", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Restored the source graph and scoped the question to the three line formulas, which uniquely identify E without assuming missing endpoint markers.\nWorked solution: The left segment has slope 1 and passes through (−3,0), giving y=x+3. The middle segment has slope 2 and y-intercept −1, giving y=2x−1. The right segment has slope −1/2 and passes through (4,0), giving y=−x/2+2. Only E has all three expressions. The source does not mark endpoint inclusion clearly, so the prompt deliberately asks about the segments away from the breakpoints.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2june:q24", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-JUN2021-Q24", "question_id": "6d879c43-fa32-59d5-8fd3-bf7d2620c678", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Specified sample standard deviation, the convention matching the source choices.\nWorked solution: The sample mean is 278/7≈39.714286. The sum of squared deviations is 2194/7≈313.428571. Divide by n−1=6 to get sample variance 1097/21≈52.238095. Half the square root is approximately 3.6138, which rounds to 3.61.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:47.350971+00", "hash": "4cb3a86bb482cbbf8499cedc4b5f11bc", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Specified sample standard deviation, the convention matching the source choices.\nWorked solution: The sample mean is 278/7≈39.714286. The sum of squared deviations is 2194/7≈313.428571. Divide by n−1=6 to get sample variance 1097/21≈52.238095. Half the square root is approximately 3.6138, which rounds to 3.61.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2june:q32", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-JUN2021-Q32", "question_id": "6ac3fdb6-0f06-5c8f-90ee-9c3e43f1cb6b", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Added “each greater than 1” to exclude the original alternatives involving 1, such as 1×11×21.\nWorked solution: The prime factorization is 231=3×7×11. Because all three factors are integers greater than 1, each must contain at least one prime factor. There are exactly three prime factors, so the three integers must be 3, 7, and 11 in some order. Their sum is 21.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:47.350971+00", "hash": "9a0875a1c40bc82cc6998c7d249b9376", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Added “each greater than 1” to exclude the original alternatives involving 1, such as 1×11×21.\nWorked solution: The prime factorization is 231=3×7×11. Because all three factors are integers greater than 1, each must contain at least one prime factor. There are exactly three prime factors, so the three integers must be 3, 7, and 11 in some order. Their sum is 21.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2june:q34", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-JUN2021-Q34", "question_id": "77400e2a-a414-5b01-857d-0c94f2e7c901", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Explicitly distinguished exact solutions from rounded approximations, resolving the B/E precision ambiguity.\nWorked solution: Use sin 2x=2sin x cos x to factor the equation as sin x(3+4cos x)=0. Its full solution is x=kπ or x=±arccos(−3/4)+2kπ, where k is an integer. Every x=−2πn is an exact solution. The values 2.42 and 3.86 are rounded approximations, not exact values of arccos(−3/4) or its other branch, so the other listed families do not consist of exact solutions.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:47.350971+00", "hash": "81d5c65b27b76d1ab8207e30ffca9df4", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Explicitly distinguished exact solutions from rounded approximations, resolving the B/E precision ambiguity.\nWorked solution: Use sin 2x=2sin x cos x to factor the equation as sin x(3+4cos x)=0. Its full solution is x=kπ or x=±arccos(−3/4)+2kπ, where k is an integer. Every x=−2πn is an exact solution. The values 2.42 and 3.86 are rounded approximations, not exact values of arccos(−3/4) or its other branch, so the other listed families do not consist of exact solutions.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2june:q39", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-JUN2021-Q39", "question_id": "b927982b-5e81-56d8-a4e4-3de4ff419aab", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Transcribed all diagram data into the stem and corrected A from 15.89 to 15.90. The wording “could” correctly accommodates the two SSA triangles.\nWorked solution: By the sine rule, sin B=12sin(28°)/7.5≈0.7511545. Thus B≈48.6905° or 131.3095°, and C≈103.3095° or 20.6905°. The area is (1/2)(12)(7.5)sin C. The two possibilities are approximately 43.7913 and 15.8994 cm², rounding to 43.79 and 15.90. Only 15.90 is listed.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:47.350971+00", "hash": "d1ccf9293d010cd7712df2bb671d027b", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Transcribed all diagram data into the stem and corrected A from 15.89 to 15.90. The wording “could” correctly accommodates the two SSA triangles.\nWorked solution: By the sine rule, sin B=12sin(28°)/7.5≈0.7511545. Thus B≈48.6905° or 131.3095°, and C≈103.3095° or 20.6905°. The area is (1/2)(12)(7.5)sin C. The two possibilities are approximately 43.7913 and 15.8994 cm², rounding to 43.79 and 15.90. Only 15.90 is listed.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2may:q22", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-MAY2021-Q22", "question_id": "427b4627-3d6c-5b2a-8490-8a7cf1272b3e", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Corrected D from “above” to “below”; the original D and E were both true. Original text is preserved in the audit backup.\nWorked solution: Factor x²−1=(x−1)(x+1). For x≠±1, f(x)=(x+3)/[(x²+1)(x+1)]. Cancellation creates a hole at x=1, with limiting y-value 1. There is one vertical asymptote, x=−1; the horizontal asymptote is y=0; and the x-intercept is −3. For x<−3 both x+3 and x+1 are negative, so f(x)>0. Only E is true after correcting D.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:47.350971+00", "hash": "bcbc1bb000273aeaec4d41f40e864c0c", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Corrected D from “above” to “below”; the original D and E were both true. Original text is preserved in the audit backup.\nWorked solution: Factor x²−1=(x−1)(x+1). For x≠±1, f(x)=(x+3)/[(x²+1)(x+1)]. Cancellation creates a hole at x=1, with limiting y-value 1. There is one vertical asymptote, x=−1; the horizontal asymptote is y=0; and the x-intercept is −3. For x<−3 both x+3 and x+1 are negative, so f(x)>0. Only E is true after correcting D.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2may:q32", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-MAY2021-Q32", "question_id": "ec415335-137b-5aa1-9159-f0f2621a503f", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Added nonverticality, which supplies the missing a+b≠0 restriction. Answer asks for the general expression, not a special parameter coincidence.\nWorked solution: The slope is (3a−3b)/(a²−b²)=3/(a+b). Nonverticality ensures a+b≠0. Substituting (a²,3a) into y=mx+c gives c=3a−3a²/(a+b)=3ab/(a+b). This is the general expression in A.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:48.689908+00", "hash": "45a4f335147669ae70b765db900d1401", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Added nonverticality, which supplies the missing a+b≠0 restriction. Answer asks for the general expression, not a special parameter coincidence.\nWorked solution: The slope is (3a−3b)/(a²−b²)=3/(a+b). Nonverticality ensures a+b≠0. Substituting (a²,3a) into y=mx+c gives c=3a−3a²/(a+b)=3ab/(a+b). This is the general expression in A.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2may:q47", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-MAY2021-Q47", "question_id": "0f3e0356-c659-54d2-a982-45ec57e1a515", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Added the normal-distribution assumption and expressed the answer as a fraction to match the printed options.\nWorked solution: A normal distribution is symmetric about its mean, with half its probability on each side. Equivalently z=(100−100)/16=0, whose cumulative probability is 0.50. The corresponding percentile is the 50th.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:48.689908+00", "hash": "1ef015a42eec2f3c8b4325427a392267", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Added the normal-distribution assumption and expressed the answer as a fraction to match the printed options.\nWorked solution: A normal distribution is symmetric about its mean, with half its probability on each side. Equivalently z=(100−100)/16=0, whose cumulative probability is 0.50. The corresponding percentile is the 50th.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2oct:q03", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-OCT2020-Q03", "question_id": "435a674f-a11f-544c-a740-04115f2b4810", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Specified degrees, the missing convention required by the source answer choices.\nWorked solution: First g(2)=3√7. Next h(3√7)=(3√7)²−3=63−3=60. Finally f(60)=−3cos60°=−3/2=−1.5. The angle unit is explicitly degrees.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:48.689908+00", "hash": "a599cab068b4bd16cb58a39d07a09e00", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Specified degrees, the missing convention required by the source answer choices.\nWorked solution: First g(2)=3√7. Next h(3√7)=(3√7)²−3=63−3=60. Finally f(60)=−3cos60°=−3/2=−1.5. The angle unit is explicitly degrees.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2oct:q22", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-OCT2020-Q22", "question_id": "030fc279-24b3-570c-b6f9-11997fb78d8b", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Specified distinct cards and one card per friend, resolving the source’s ambiguous distribution rule.\nWorked solution: Choose the first friend’s card in 8 ways, the second’s in 7, then 6, 5, and 4 ways for the remaining friends. The product is 8×7×6×5×4=6720. This is P(8,5), because both cards and recipients are distinct.", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 19:50:48.689908+00", "hash": "16a28d33641d9eba2ed698a54dbac0de", "status": "excluded", "note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Specified distinct cards and one card per friend, resolving the source’s ambiguous distribution rule.\nWorked solution: Choose the first friend’s card in 8 ways, the second’s in 7, then 6, 5, and 4 ways for the remaining friends. The product is 8×7×6×5×4=6720. This is P(8,5), because both cards and recipients are distinct.\nDisposition 2026-10-15: Intentionally removed by instructor curriculum request; retain source evidence only, not available practice."}, {"id": "est2-papers-2026-09-26:l2oct:q31", "track_id": "est2", "source_code": "EST2-L2-OCT2020-Q31", "question_id": "c7bdeee7-9368-58cd-a5b4-8f9ac3a31302", "review_status": "ready", "review_note": "Rechecked 2026-09-28. Original source image decrypted, hash checked, and visually inspected. Corrected choice E’s arithmetic and explicitly state